<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gulf War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1990–1991</span> · Also known as Persian Gulf War, First Gulf War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gulf War was the conflict that followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>'s invasion and annexation of Kuwait in August 1990. A coalition of 35 states led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> assembled forces in Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and, after an air campaign from January 1991, drove the Iraqi army out of Kuwait in a short ground offensive in February. Iraq remained under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a> and no-fly zones for over a decade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gulf-war.jpg" alt="Gulf War" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: US Air Force · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:USAF_F-16A_F-15C_F-15E_Desert_Storm_edit2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
